  "note": "Tier 1, from the decks: a two-player Commander game (903.2) exercising the command_zone question of 903.9a. A's deck is Isamaru, Hound of Konda (its commander, a legendary creature, 903.3) and 99 Plains; B's is Krenko, Mob Boss (its commander) and 98 Mountains and one Lightning Bolt: 100 cards each including the commander (903.5a); every card's color identity is within its commander's (903.4, 903.4c: a basic land's reminder text adds nothing; 903.5c, 903.5d: Plains produce {W} for white Isamaru, Mountains {R} for red Krenko). The commanders begin in the command zone (903.6; card table `from: command`), the libraries are the other 99 cards, life totals are 40 (903.7, 103.4c). A plays first (103.8a: no draw on turn 1), plays a Plains and casts Isamaru from the command zone (903.8); on turn 2 B draws, plays a Mountain and kills Isamaru with Lightning Bolt (704.5g); A then chooses to put Isamaru from its graveyard into the command zone (903.9a). The file was generated by a short script (a bulk edit of the 200-card table and shuffle orders) and written from the specification, the pinned rules and the pinned Oracle text alone.",
